by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-01T15:11:47Z

@MatTheCat sorry, I missed your comment and pushed before reading it. You are right, and I switched the pull request to your approach.

It is better for a reason my own review had already demonstrated without me drawing the conclusion. The previous shape hid the toolbar with a class and relied on JavaScript to take it off again, and when I enumerated the terminal outcomes of `loadToolbar()` there were four paths that never removed it: `xhr.status === 0`, the early return when `sfToolbarMainContent-<token>` is missing, the early return when the response carries no `sf-toolbarreset` markup, and Cancel during a retry wait. In each of those the toolbar did not merely flash, it silently did not exist, which is worse than the bug being fixed. I had centralised the removal into a single closure to cover them. Your version has nothing to remove, so none of those paths can exist at all. Deleting the failure mode beats fixing it.

Your reproduction on an emulated 2G connection is also better evidence than what I had, which was markup ordering plus driving the emitted JavaScript through a fake DOM.

Two adjustments to the snippet. The empty `script` needs the script nonce, otherwise a strict policy drops it and the blocking effect disappears silently; the file already uses `{% if csp_script_nonce is defined and csp_script_nonce %}` a few lines below. And the `role="toolbar"` in your snippet is the 8.1 and 8.2 form, this branch has `role="region"`.

The diff is now five lines added and two removed, with no class, no inline style and no JavaScript involved. I verified the rendered order and both nonces by rendering the template through Twig and applying the same newline stripping `WebDebugToolbarListener::injectToolbar()` does. `./phpunit src/Symfony/Bundle/WebProfilerBundle` gives `OK (160 tests, 471 assertions)`.

One consequence worth recording: the page's `DOMContentLoaded` now waits for the toolbar stylesheet. Same development server, toolbar-only, so I think that is a fair price for removing the whole class of stuck-hidden bugs, but it is a real change and it is in the description.
